{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1541155-about-the-multiverse","id":1541155,"title":"About the multiverse","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-28T19:17:43-07:00","id":1541155,"title":"About the multiverse","content":"are there realms beyond creation/the wyld? some of the lore implies that there is a greater multiverse. is this true?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27683-bernese","name":"Bernese","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T20:00:36-07:00","id":1541160,"title":"","content":"Strange stars, alien worlds, and devastated ruins floating in the void, sure. I don't know if it constitutes a multiverse, and a lot of those journeys are segments of adventures that focus back on Creation in one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T06:17:50-07:00","id":1541225,"title":"","content":"It depends on what somebody means by multiverse. Like, just going by the base game there is Creation surrounded by the endless chaos of the Wyld, where Yu-Shan, the Underworld, and Malfeas constitute different planes of existence. That alone matches certain connotations of the term.<br /> <br /> There do seem to be ideas of other planes of existence akin to those well-known ones, which may or may not be as firmly rooted to Creation. Getimian Exalted explicitly do not come from alternate timelines, they're purely hypothetic until the Exaltation makes them real, but the association with Oramus and why he was able to contribute to an Essence that could do such a thing could be taken as suggesting that his powers can engage with some other realities that are a bit more like things (even if that becomes complicated by the element of him being attached to unreal things).<br /> <br /> Third Edition inclines a bit towards an approach of &quot;more than is dreamt of in your philosophies&quot;, that it's possible for things to show up that don't quite fit into the neatly established categories. <br /> <br /> But I think the general presentation of that is kind of pulpy and weird, where the term &quot;multiverse&quot; might imply clear definitions and comprehensible arrangement. <br /> <br /> So there probably isn't a multiverse in the way that most people would immediately go to if they heard the term, but there's still a capacity for things to come in from cosmological parts unknown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T18:33:13-07:00","id":1541370,"title":"","content":"Like Isator Said, it depends on what you mean.<br /> If it's just having multiple dimensions, then yes, Exalted does have that.I'd not call that a &quot;multiverse&quot; though - there may be other &quot;dimensions&quot;, but they are not really truly separate, alternate/parallel worlds, but rather a single, big verse with distinct &quot;subspaces&quot;.<br /> There's the infinite sea of the Wyld, with Creation at the center, and some other, smaller and bigger bubbles of semi-reality maybe floating around. Yu-Shan, Malfeas and Underworld are contained dimensions tied to Creation proper, spread &quot;over&quot; and &quot;under&quot; it. There's also Elsewhere, but that's a really weird case, and i'd rather treat it not as a real dimension, but more like a state of existence.<br /> Now, as for something more like multiverse, canon says nothing about. The closest we'd get would be probably the Well of Urd, but even that is not really described as leading to more realities, but more as containing many possibilities within. Those are not exactly the same things. Also, Well of Urd was a 2nd edition thing. If it even makes a comeback in 3e (uncertain, but possible, considering its some ties to Abyssals and Deathlords), it's definitely going to be changed/downplayed from even that.<br /> There's also Oramus, but the way he is all about impossibilities makes it really doubtful that whatever he is accessing is actually real.<br /> The only book that actually does speak about other realities, Shards of a Broken Dream (the alternate realities setting book for 2e) is considered to be non-canon, and completely separate as far as main setting is concerned.<br /> Now, on the other hand, there's also nothing in the settings that says that other realities/parallel worlds/alternate dimensions do <i>not</i> exist. They might. The settings neither confirms nor deny that possibilty. If you really want it to be true, it's up to you to decide how they'd fit in the greater picture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T13:03:25-07:00","id":1541403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1541155-about-the-multiverse?p=1541370#post1541370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, as for something more like multiverse, canon says nothing about. The closest we'd get would be probably the Well of Urd,</div> </div> </div> </div>Udr. It's full of chocolate!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}